Z||000004||fiero56||07-21-2001||06:47 PM||||Was waiting at a light so I could go through and take the highway entrance ramp about 1/8 mile up the road, a newer 325i pulled alongside. A favorite of people in the area is to blast out of the light in the left lane and cut over to the right in time to hit the entrance ramp. I figured that was the intent of this 325 with two guys in their early 20s so I decided I was going to try and prevent this. As I launched they decided it was a race. They had that auto 325 screaming, and I lost a little ground having to shift. I was very surprised to find neither of us were able to pull away. By the time the entrance ramp came up, they had about 3 feet on me. Turned out they weren't taking the highway just wanted to go at it. I was surprised, and sort of asked myself why I needed a new 2.8 if my 178K mile slight rod-knocking 2.8e could keep up with a 325i. If that Bimmer had been a stick, I'm sure they would have wasted me.||||reg||1
Z||000005||firstfiero||07-22-2001||11:12 AM||||    Being a former bmw owner I can say that the 3 series...unless it's and M class..isn't that fast. It's more of a quick excellent handeling car. You shouldn't have lost ground shifting....You need to learn how to slam shift!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
